# ─── credentials and environment ───────────────────────────────────────────
# See docs/08-security-privacy.md §7.1. These exist from the initial commit:
# a .gitignore added on day 40 does not protect the first 39 days, and git
# history is append-only in exactly the way the map is (D-020).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials
.aws/

# ─── agent + editor tooling config ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The O-005 class. Agent tool configuration is a credential-bearing surface —
# a live AWS credential pair was found inlined in a permission allowlist — and
# it is machine-local by nature: nothing in it needs sharing with a repo that
# has one contributor. Deny by default, allow by exception (D-154).
# NOTE the trailing /* rather than / on .claude — this is load-bearing.
# `.claude/` excludes the DIRECTORY, so git never descends into it and no
# later ! rule can re-admit anything inside. `.claude/*` excludes the
# contents, which leaves the directory walkable so the exceptions below work.
.claude/*
.cursor/
.vscode/
*.local.json
**/settings.local.json

# ...allow by exception: the /tickets skill genuinely belongs in version
# control. Re-admitted explicitly, and reviewed on the way in.
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**

# ─── generated, environment-specific ───────────────────────────────────────
# amplify_outputs.json is ignored because it is generated per-environment,
# NOT because it is sensitive. Stated so nobody "fixes" this by deleting the
# line, and nobody treats a leak of it as an incident.
amplify_outputs.json
.amplify/
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── os / editor noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
